Let a local stream be reset after its FIN is sent, until the FIN is ACKed.

RFC 9000 Section 3.1 allows RESET_STREAM in the "Data Sent" state: the FIN
has been sent but not every byte and the FIN are acknowledged. Upstream
refuses that reset, because its "already closed" check reads fin_offset,
which is set only from received frames, and because a sent FIN has already
removed the stream from the output list, so an accepted reset would never
be formatted. The draft-18 subgroup DELIVERY_TIMEOUT needs this reset.

- picoquic_reset_stream_at refuses only when no reset is pending and the
  sent bytes and FIN are all acknowledged (sent_offset), the terminal
  "Data Recvd" state. It clears the application stream context only when
  it accepts, and puts the stream back on the output list.
- It refuses a Reliable Size above the stream's Final Size with
  PICOQUIC_ERROR_OFFSET_TOO_BIG (the upstream code and value). Bytes
  already queued but not yet sent count toward the Final Size, since they
  are sent before the reset; picowt_reset_stream() can reset a stream
  whose preamble is still queued.
- The scheduler keeps a stream whose FIN is sent while a reset is pending,
  so a reliable reset waiting for its prefix ACK is still sent later.
- When an ACK completes every byte and the FIN while the reset is still
  unsent, the stream has reached "Data Recvd": the reset is dropped and
  the stream retires as a completed one. A reset already sent still waits
  for its own ACK.
- An ACK of an empty non-FIN STREAM frame records nothing, instead of
  underflowing to a SACK range that covers the whole stream.
- ACKs of RESET_STREAM_AT reach the existing retirement handler, which now
  consumes the Reliable Size field so later frames in the same packet are
  still parsed.
- A received RESET_STREAM_AT whose Reliable Size exceeds its Final Size
  closes the connection with FRAME_ENCODING_ERROR, as
  draft-ietf-quic-reliable-stream-reset Section 4 requires.

Applies to picoquic 55b473e207e436d06ea9a2895cc1fc555d42c81c, after 0001.
Tests: adapters/picoquic/tests/test_pq_reset_after_fin.c (CTest
pq_reset_after_fin), with constructed stream/SACK rows and packet rows over
the simulated links.

